# Vulnerability details

### Impact
This vulnerability allows users to manipulate asset prices and liquidate themselves, potentially leading to unfair profit generation and destabilization of the asset pricing mechanism within the platform.

### Proof of Concept
In `VaultManagerV2.sol:205`, the function [liquidate](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/VaultManagerV2.sol#L205) permits users to liquidate their own positions. This can be exploited by a user who deposits a small amount into a kerosene vault and a larger amount into endogenous collateral vaults. Due to the calculation mechanism of kerosene vaults, which scales the price with the total value locked (TVL), this results in an inflated kerosene price. The user can then mint DYAD tokens proportional to the inflated USD value of their NFT and subsequently liquidate themselves to another NFT, effectively bypassing withdrawal restrictions.

