# Vulnerability details

## ISSUE

In [`DeployV2.s.sol`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/main/script/deploy/Deploy.V2.s.sol), a new version of the `Licenser` is [deployed](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/script/deploy/Deploy.V2.s.sol#L39). The [DYAD](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/main/src/core/Dyad.sol) contract (0x305B58c5F6B5b6606fb13edD11FbDD5e532d5A26) uses the [old Licenser implementation](https://etherscan.io/address/0x305b58c5f6b5b6606fb13edd11fbdd5e532d5a26#readContract#F5) (0xd8bA5e720Ddc7ccD24528b9BA3784708528d0B85). This Licenser contract was used during construction of the DYAD contract and this is what the DYAD contract will read from when performing checks (i.e. checking a licensed vault/vaultManager) before minting tokens. There is no function to update the Licenser in the DYAD contract.

If this new Licenser version is deployed and a vault manager is added to it, it will break calls to DYAD as the modifier [`licensedVaultManager()`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/Dyad.sol#L20-L23) will still check in the [old implementation](https://github.com/code-423n4/2024-04-dyad/blob/cd48c684a58158de444b24854ffd8f07d046c31b/src/core/Dyad.sol#L9) (The DYAD contract cannot update the Licenser).

```solidity

    //@audit-info - Modifier checks if caller is licensed. Caller is `vaultManagerV2`
    modifier licensedVaultManager() {
        if (!licenser.isLicensed(msg.sender)) revert NotLicensed();
        _;
    }

```

This will cause the `licenser.isLicensed()` check (in the modifier) to return false since it cannot read from the new Licenser. This will lead to reverts in the `mint()` function of the DYAD contract.

