The `VaultManagerV2::liquidate` function erroneously calls `Dyad::burn` on `msg.sender` address, resulting in the burning of DYAD tokens belonging to the caller of the function.

The purpose of the liquidation process is to resolve undercollateralized positions by either selling off or transferring the collateralized assets to cover the outstanding debt or obligations associated with the loan. Burning the minted tokens of `msg.sender` does not contribute to this goal. Instead, it penalizes the caller by causing a loss of their assets without effectively addressing the underlying issue of undercollateralization.

