## Proof of Concept

According to the [docs](https://dyadstable.notion.site/DYAD-design-outline-v6-3fa96f99425e458abbe574f67b795145) 
"The liquidator burns a quantity of DYAD equal to the target Note’s DYAD minted balance, and in return receives an equivalent value plus a 20% bonus of the target Note’s backing colateral, which the liquidator can direct to any other Note, usually their own."

However, when the liquidator burns his dyad to repay the liquidated note's debt, there will be a mismatch between his balanceOf and his note's `mintedDyad`, drawing him unable to redeem/withdraw, unless a third party transfers him dyad to match his note's `mintedDyad` or burn his mintedDyad from their dyad's balance.

